9\u2026`, and `int()` just drops everything after the decimal point. That loses a cent on the subtotal before tax or discount runs. The same thing happens to `0.29` (\u00d73 gave 86 instead of 87) and `4.35` (434 instead of 435).\n\n**Fix:** `to_cents` now turns the amount into a `Decimal` via `str()`, so `19.99` stays exactly `19.99` with no float error. It multiplies by 100 and rounds half away from zero to a whole number of cents. Prices with exactly two decimal places convert exactly. Prices with more decimals now round instead of being cut off. No callers changed; `Line.cents()` is the only one.\n\n**Verification:** the system Python has no pytest and won't allow a global install, so I made a venv at `/tmp/venv`. `/tmp/venv/bin/python -m pytest tests -q` gave 5 passed.\n\nI didn't add a separate test for `to_cents`; the existing subtotal tests already catch this bug.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 0, "replies_ok": 6, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 77725, "requests_cache_write": 18058, "requests_cost_usd": 0.149991, "requests_count": 6, "requests_input_uncached": 14, "requests_output": 2205, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-multistep:claude-opus-5-5:trial5", "run_seed": 20261014, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 9, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-13T03:24:59.007739+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 28.722, "t_checker_s": 0.381, "t_env_setup_s": 0.001, "task": "trig-omp-multistep", "task_calls": 0, "thinking_mode": "off", "thinking_sent": ["none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none"], "timeout_s": 360, "tmpdir_leaked_dirs": 0, "token_basis": "proxy_measured", "token_basis_main": "estimated", "token_basis_proxy": "proxy_measured", "tokens": 2219, "tokens_cache_read": 77725, "tokens_cache_write": 18058, "tokens_fresh": 2219, "tokens_input_uncached": 14, "tokens_main_cache_read": 77725